xnu: split the GMU bring-up so the CX write can be blamed on its own

The gmu=2 boot reset the machine before a single byte reached the log ring, so
two writes are still both suspects: the CX GBIF halt clear and the CM3_SYSRESET
release. Mode 3 clears the halt and then stops, leaving CM3 held in reset, so
one boot separates "the kgsl write is fatal" from "the firmware faults on boot".

The selftest covers the new stop point; nothing else changes.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
index d8269ea..d164800 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -395,6 +395,16 @@ sweet_adreno_gmu_load(volatile void *gpucc, volatile void *gmu, volatile void *k
 	}
 	IOLog("SWEET ADRENO: CX GBIF halt cleared\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * mode 3 = 走到这里就停：清完 halt 但不放复位。上一轮 gmu=2 在整机复位前
+	 * 一个字都没进日志环，所以那两次写哪个是凶手分不清；3 把 CX 那次单独切出来。
+	 */
+	if (mode == 3) {
+		IOLog("SWEET ADRENO: gmu load stopped after the CX halt clear (mode=3,"
+		    " CM3 still in reset)\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	sweet_adreno_snapshot(gpucc, gmu, "pre-gmu-boot");
 	sweet_adreno_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_OFF(SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET), 0);
 	{
